          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for to feel relieved, then the Marathi for to be choked up."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ओढ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ओढ — oḍh — \"a longing; a pull\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सुट्टीत गावाची ओढ लागते. suṭṭīt gāvācī oḍh lāgte. In the holidays one longs for the village."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ओढ (oḍh) लागणे, to feel drawn to, with the genitive: घराची ओढ (oḍh). It belongs with ओढणे, to pull."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ओढ (oḍh) is a Marathi noun beside ओढणे, \"to pull\", which goes back to the reconstructed avakaḍḍhati, \"pulls away\" (CDIAL 14245)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
